# scripts/mutate.py writes one of these beside a file while it is mutated, and
# removes it on a clean exit. One that survives is a run that was killed, and
# the next run recovers from it — but it must never be committed, because a
# committed backup is a half-mutated tree that looks like source.
*.mutate-backup

# scripts/ became importable in v0.70 (stagelock.py is shared by three runners),
# so running any of them now leaves bytecode beside the sources. Never source.
__pycache__/
*.selftest-backup
